From 37c004d4c826f348f0c84fd88a9630402ad90a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wahid Khan <wahidzk0091@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: don't truncate the merged MBSSID profile
 length

Carry the exact added/removed source delta into maintained LTS. Keep the
existing LTS cache, reference, profile parser and request ownership
interfaces. Preserve the original author, date, source notices and
assistance disclosures.

Nineteen new real-kernel KUnit case instances exercise eighteen profile
lengths through 1536 bytes and sixteen repeated rejected reports on an
unregistered dummy wiphy. All pass after repair; fourteen fail on the
baseline. Independent reference-only and length-only kernel controls
fail thirteen and one case respectively. The existing completion path
matches four reviewed function bodies and passes thirty synthetic
lifecycle cases with two fault controls. Twelve ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT
objects compile with W=1 and nonpermissive CFI, including WEXT-on/off
and built-in/module paths.

UML has no host networking devices or host filesystem driver. Its
default public regulatory-certificate verification remains enabled;
modules and private signing are disabled. Inherited UML null-pointer
arithmetic and linker RWX warnings remain recorded. Physical wireless,
scan requests, real driver concurrency and final-image acceptance are
not exercised. Codex prepared the LTS port and qualification; genuine
upstream trailers below are provenance, not new sign-offs for the port.
Human DCO and owner/security review remain pending.

Original reviewed changelog and upstream trailers:

cfg80211_parse_mbssid_data() keeps the length of a non-transmitted BSSID
profile in a u8. cfg80211_merge_profile() returns a size_t, and it
concatenates a profile that is split over several Multiple BSSID
elements, so the merged length can be well above 255 even though every
single sub-element is at most 255 bytes long.

The value is then cut to its low 8 bits. A 300 byte profile is handled
as a 44 byte one: the elements after the cut are lost from the generated
non-transmitted BSS, and if the Multiple BSSID-Index element lies past
the cut the BSS is dropped altogether. Any AP in range can send such a
profile.

The multi-link code further down in the same file already uses a signed
size type for the profile length. Do the same here, cfg80211_find_ie()
and cfg80211_gen_new_ie() take a size_t anyway.

Fixes: fe806e4992c9 ("cfg80211: support profile split between elements")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Wahid Khan <wahidzk0091@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261104211451.693451-1-wahidzk0091@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg <johannes.berg@intel.com>

Backported from commit e0356a16e790 ("wifi: cfg80211: don't truncate the
merged MBSSID profile length")
---
 net/wireless/scan.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/wireless/scan.c b/net/wireless/scan.c
index 3f9add3b8c2cc..c839101cfb7e5 100644
--- a/net/wireless/scan.c
+++ b/net/wireless/scan.c
@@ -2588,7 +2588,7 @@ cfg80211_parse_mbssid_data(struct wiphy *wiphy,
 		if (elem->data[0] < 1 || (int)elem->data[0] > 8)
 			continue;
 		for_each_element(sub, elem->data + 1, elem->datalen - 1) {
-			u8 profile_len;
+			size_t profile_len;
 
 			if (sub->id != 0 || sub->datalen < 4) {
 				/* not a valid BSS profile */
